  "worked_solution": "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}\u2061x={csc}^{2}\u2061x.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2+3{x}^{2}+2{cot}^{2}\u2061x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2(1+{cot}^{2}\u2061x)+3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2{csc}^{2}\u2061x+3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-2\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x+{x}^{3}){|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{3}-[-2\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+{(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{3}] \\\\  & =-0+\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{8}+2(1)-\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{64} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
